From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vo_avfoundation: add the AVFoundation video output

Adds vo=avfoundation for iOS and tvOS. It presents decoded frames,
VideoToolbox or software, on the AVSampleBufferDisplayLayer whose address
is passed as --wid, as timed sample buffers. It never scales, tone-maps or
re-renders the picture apart from the Picture in Picture subtitle
composite. Creation fails cleanly without --wid (logged at verbose while
mpv probes outputs), so autoprobing moves on.

Formats: VideoToolbox, NV12, yuv420p, P010 and 10-bit and 12-bit planar
4:2:0; mpv converts anything else. A VideoToolbox device registered as
"avfoundation" lets hwdec=videotoolbox decode straight into frames the
output accepts; it is removed and the device list destroyed at teardown.

Timing: --avfoundation-presentation=host (the tvOS default) presents at
mpv's target host times on a timebase that follows the host clock;
media (the default elsewhere, needed by Picture in Picture) presents at
media times on a timebase the output anchors and slews to mpv's schedule.
Frames that cannot be enqueued by 4 ms before their target are dropped and
counted. A seek keeps the last picture until a new one arrives; the layer
is recovered after the app becomes active again and when the renderer
fails. A subtitle sample that misses its frame for any reason is rendered
again with the next one.

Subtitles go to a separate layer laid out in display space, or, with
--avfoundation-pip-composite-osd=yes, into the pictures in frame space.
--avfoundation-queue-lead-ms sets how early frames are handed over
(128 ms). --avfoundation-composite-osd is accepted and has no effect.

The output is the meson feature vo-avfoundation and is registered first in
the video output list. It needs iOS or tvOS 17 or later.

Applies to mpv v0.41.0 with Vivid's earlier patches.

Licence: this patch is part of Vivid's Lucid Engine patch series for mpv.
